From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:12:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sdhci-pci-gli: runtime suspend the J604's idle
 GL9755 by default

The GL9755 card reader of the J604 (MacBook Pro 14-inch, M4) sits alone
on an APCIe port and stays in D0 with its link up while the slot is
empty. Runtime PM for it already exists behind gl9755_runtime_pm, off
by default: the controller then runtime suspends to D3hot, with the card
found by polling once a second, as the slot has no card detect GPIO and
the card detect interrupt is masked in runtime suspend.

On the J604 that path was measured: runtime suspended and D3hot in
18 of 20 samples with the switch on, back in D0 with it off, and no
sdhci or mmc error lines.

Turn the switch into on / off / auto and make auto the default: on for
the J604 (apple,j604), off on every other machine as before.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-pci-gli.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-pci-gli.c b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-pci-gli.c
index 21cca237d1..87ca343623 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-pci-gli.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-pci-gli.c
@@ -21,10 +21,24 @@
 #include "cqhci.h"
 #include "sdhci-uhs2.h"
 
-static bool gl9755_runtime_pm;
-module_param(gl9755_runtime_pm, bool, 0644);
+static int gl9755_runtime_pm = -1;
+module_param(gl9755_runtime_pm, int, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(gl9755_runtime_pm,
-		 "Runtime suspend an idle GL9755, polling for a card once a second; read when the device is bound (default: off)");
+		 "Runtime suspend an idle GL9755, polling for a card once a second; read when the device is bound: 1 on, 0 off, -1 auto = on for the MacBook Pro J604 (default: -1)");
+
+/*
+ * The J604 (MacBook Pro 14-inch, M4) has its GL9755 alone on an APCIe
+ * port and no use for it while the slot is empty; macOS keeps that link
+ * idle. Other boards keep their runtime PM as it was, unless asked.
+ */
+static bool gl9755_want_runtime_pm(void)
+{
+	int v = READ_ONCE(gl9755_runtime_pm);
+
+	if (v >= 0)
+		return v;
+	return of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j604");
+}
 
 /*  Genesys Logic extra registers */
 #define SDHCI_GLI_9750_WT         0x800
@@ -1601,7 +1615,7 @@ static int gli_probe_slot_gl9755(struct sdhci_pci_slot *slot)
 	 * Runtime suspend masks the card detect interrupt, and the slot has
 	 * no card detect GPIO, so a card is then found by polling.
 	 */
-	if (gl9755_runtime_pm) {
+	if (gl9755_want_runtime_pm()) {
 		host->mmc->caps |= MMC_CAP_NEEDS_POLL;
 		slot->chip->allow_runtime_pm = true;
 	}
-- 
2.43.0

